<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Definitions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
    <EntityComponents>

<!-- Hangar Plane Behaviors: applied to the Player-WW2-* prefab parked inside a
     Hangar shell, not the Hangar building itself. Passive — no AI piloting,
     just post-spawn cleanup (unstick from static).

     2026-08-22: recreated after being deleted earlier the same session — static
     spawning was tried instead (no Behaviour at all) to rule out SetGridToDynamic
     as the source of spawn-time collision damage, but that made the facing go
     backwards again (the working facing was previously only ever seen together
     with dynamic conversion + the 7.5m SpawnGroup position shift, so dynamic
     conversion itself, not just the position, appears to matter for facing).
     Root cause of the collision damage turned out to be height, not physics
     drop as first assumed — the plane was spawning low enough to launch up into
     the hangar ceiling on becoming dynamic, then falling and taking damage from
     that impact. Fixed by raising FC20 1.25m in the SpawnGroup, not by removing
     this behavior. The engine/propeller disable attempt is still gone; not
     restored here. -->
		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
            <Id>
                <TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>WW2-Behavior-HangarPlane-FC20</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <Description>

			[RivalAI Behavior]
			[BehaviorName:Passive]

			[Triggers:WW2-Trigger-UnStatic]

			</Description>
        </EntityComponent>

<!-- 2026-08-22: same pattern extended to the rest of the Hangar roster (Re2001/MS406/
     Potez630). Each is just the shared UnStatic trigger, identical to FC20's — no
     per-plane engine/propeller disable, matching the decision made for FC20. -->
		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
            <Id>
                <TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>WW2-Behavior-HangarPlane-Re2001</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <Description>

			[RivalAI Behavior]
			[BehaviorName:Passive]

			[Triggers:WW2-Trigger-UnStatic]

			</Description>
        </EntityComponent>

		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
